Today I read an article about the problems faced by Gen Z. It mentioned a girl who worked in the IT field. She had been working under heavy pressure and workload, so she decided to leave her job. A psychologist 
explained that because of such situations, many Gen Z individuals tend to seek deeper commitments elsewhere. Since Gen Z lives in constant connectivity, this often leads to exhaustion. As a result, people are now 
trying to find ways to relieve stress, such as opening up to their close ones.

